  "query_preview": "..\n(Saturday through next Thursday)\nIssued at 1251 PM CDT Thu Jul 23 2026\n\nMid-level ridging will dominate much of the Central and Western US \nthrough the long term period keeping South-Central Texas seasonably \nhot and dry. With a drier airmass in place over the region, skies \nwill are forecast to partly cloudy to mostly sunny each day through \nlate next week with a light to moderate south-southeasterly wind. \nWidespread highs will mainly be in the mid and upper 90s this \nweekend, then begin to creep up heading into next week. Heat indices \nwill still be in the 100 to 105 degree range for many through the \nperiod.",
